WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.205
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.205 --> 00:00:04.240
about optimizing with
recommenders, Google Cloud

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.970
certifications, and
data center security.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.610
I'm Priyanka Vergadia,
and welcome to "This Week

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.400
in Cloud," where we serve
you the lowest latency

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.760
news from the safety of home.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.520
With recommenders, our goal
is to suggest quick, easy ways

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.160
to optimize your cloud
for price, performance,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.210
and security.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.160
Several recommenders are
already available today,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.060
including Virtual Machine
Recommender, Viral Insights,

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.500
and IAM Recommender.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.010
And now we're releasing the
beta of our new Recommendations

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.460
Hub, which highlights proactive
recommendations in one place

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.010
for you to view and act on.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.500
Two years ago, we
created a gaming solution

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.530
to bring real world games
to life with the Google Maps

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.530
Platform.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.070
While the initial release was
with a limited group of game

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.460
studios, we plan to expand
to independent game studios

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.700
and developers.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.630
So we focused on building a
scalable infrastructure that

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.460
would support all developers.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.670
And now we're releasing our
Google Maps Platform gaming

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:03.190
solution to all mobile
game developers,

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.740
to create engaging,
immersive, real world games.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.640
Check out the blog to learn
more and try it for yourself.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.220
Our Google Cloud training allows
you to build cloud skills,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.210
while our certifications help
organizations find expert cloud

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.050
talent.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.140
We are continually working to
improve our learning paths,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.390
and now we're announcing
three new initiatives.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.560
We are introducing Google
Cloud Skill Badges,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.110
so you can show off
your demonstrated skills

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.310
and expertise.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:36.270
We're offering six-week programs
to help experienced cloud

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.390
professionals prepare for
the certification exams.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.130
And since our exam centers
are currently closed,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.700
we have created
online-proctored testing

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.670
for three of the
certification exams.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.270
At Google Cloud, we tend to
obsess about data security.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.700
And we offer plenty of
products and services

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.470
to help our customers
secure their data.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.380
But we're just as
focused when it

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.740
comes to physical security
of our data centers.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.840
After a series of
checks and approvals,

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.600
my teammate Stephanie
Wong was given permission

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.770
to visit an actual data center
and create a video showcasing

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.860
how safe and secure
your data really is.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.830
In this video, Stephanie will
show off the six security

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.710
layers, from the secure
perimeter to the data center

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:23.830
floor, that fewer than
1% of Googlers ever see.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.010
It's a pretty cool
behind-the-scenes look,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.450
so be sure to check it out.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.940
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.470
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.760
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.770
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.240
We'll see you in the cloud.

